  "subject": "📱 Axios Finish Line: Screen-time upside",
  "date": "Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:29:26 -0400",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🏃 Plus: Kindness on the run | Thursday, October 15, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Oct 15, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 318 words … 1 min. Copy edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: Upside of logging on \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Technology often gets blamed for making us lonelier and more isolated. But the internet can also help us feel less alone by bringing people together.\n\n Why it matters: Online communities connect people who might never otherwise cross paths — or even speak the same language — through shared interests and experiences. 🧮 By the numbers: Some 4 in 10 Americans — across all age groups — belong to an online community, according to a new Pew Research Center survey . Think online book clubs, parenting forums, TV show discussion groups or cancer support groups.\n\n 70% of members say these communities have added value to their lives, and 63% say their most-visited group offers something they couldn't find offline. 36% say their online community also brings people together through in-person gatherings. Zoom in: Research reveals some of the benefits of these groups.\n\n A 2025 review of 100 studies found that online support groups can help people with chronic illnesses better adjust to their conditions. 🔎 The intrigue: Online socializing is often dismissed as a less-than-ideal substitute for in-person interaction. But online and in-person relationships may actually complement each other.\n\n A small 2026 study found that in-person support matters more for happiness. But people with strong online support also tend to have stronger real-life connections. The bottom line: Find your corner of the internet.\n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM AXIOS\r\n\n \r\n Find where your team is misaligned \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Simplify Workshop shows your team where it is misaligned and why it keeps happening.\n\n Everyone leaves with one aligned set of priorities and a real kill list, built on the Confront, Delete, Amplify method. The whole team works through it together.\n\n Learn more about the Workshop \n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 👋 Kindness to go! \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Doing good can be refreshingly simple — like this example from reader Ray Cunningham of Issaquah, Wash., who turned a random act of kindness into a habit:\n\n \"Whenever I'm out for a run, I give a wave to everyone whom I meet along the way, whether they are walking, running or cycling. Just a simple acknowledgment that we're in this together as a community. I've noticed over time that many of those who've seen me before start giving me waves back.\" \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
